data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_07849611bef88923006aa6fffd3fac87d29fcd317250b84fdb","logprobs":[],"output_index":1,"sequence_number":170,"text":"A unicorn is a mythical horse-like creature, typically depicted with a single spiraled horn, symbolizing purity, grace, and magic in folklore, art, and literature across diverse cultures worldwide and timeless.\n\nBased on the Wikipedia \"History of Ireland\" article: Irish history spans prehistoric settlement and the rise of Gaelic Celtic culture, transformed by Christianization, Viking and Norman incursions, long periods of English rule with plantations and penal laws, and tragedies like the Great Famine that caused mass death and emigration. In the 20th century Ireland achieved partial independence (1922) and partition, endured the Troubles in Northern Ireland until the 1998 Good Friday Agreement, and the Republic later modernized economically and socially—joining the EU, experiencing the Celtic Tiger boom, a 2008 financial crisis, and subsequent recovery."}

